      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] \nThis test verifies the failure path for `cros_flash_physical_protect_now(..., false)`, but omits the `all\u003dtrue` branch. \n\nTesting the `true` branch is critical here to enforce **Test Oracle Integrity** and prevent masking bugs. There is currently a state-corruption bug in `cros_flash_rtkfp_protect_now()` where `data-\u003eall_protected \u003d 1;` is executed *unconditionally* before checking the return value of `cros_flash_rtkfp_protect_at_boot()`. \n\nIf you add the `true` case, the test will correctly fail (since `get_protect_flags` will erroneously return `EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ALL_NOW` instead of `0` due to the corrupted state). \n\nPlease add test cases for both `true` and `false` to ensure all branches are isolated, and fix the underlying driver bug in a prerequisite CL.\n\n```c\n\tzassert_equal(cros_flash_physical_protect_now(cros_flash_dev, true),\n\t\t      -EIO);\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/e19ef43e-d24a-477a-b05a-91146923d2b0)",
